{
  "schema": "trial/1",
  "trial": "P-33",
  "question": "Can the issue a pull request closes be read from a draft, an open, a merged and a closed-unmerged pull request alike, with its opening actor; and does a pull request to a branch that is not the default one carry it? Can who last changed the draft flag be read?",
  "pass": "Yes to the first and last (section 6): each of a draft, an open, a merged and a closed-unmerged pull request whose description says 'Closes #N' is read with the issue N in closingIssuesReferences and with its author, and the timeline's ReadyForReviewEvent and ConvertToDraftEvent name who changed the draft flag and when. A pull request to a base that is not the default branch is tried: if it carries no reference, section 6's fallback is taken, the issue Lifecycle serves the default branch only, and the fixture says so. A closed pull request that keeps its reference is read like an open one; if it lost it, closes would be counted by the work's branch name. The merged case is read on the default branch, where a closing reference can act.",
  "repo": "combsmith/software-factory-canary",
  "ran_at": "2026-10-20T21:14:27Z",
  "exchanges": [
